  "conclusions": [
    "CLinguist is root+20C. Its vtable is not a CObject serialization table; slot2 is SetText.",
    "Text maps +4/+C/+18 are 8-byte std::map headers. A5F520 returns node+10 pair; pair key is int at+0 and mapped std::vector<pair<int,CString>> begins+4. Inner begin/end are vector+0/+4; stride8.",
    "Definition maps +20/+34/+3C/+54 use node+10 int key and a 32-byte LanguageInfo at node+14. All four CString and four scalar fields are preserved; original Save serializes only the documented subset.",
    "SetText(this,textId,languageId,CString&,bool usePersistentMap) returns AL and ret16. false selects +C; true selects +4. It does not mark modified.",
    "CommitWorkingText A54E00 / vslot41 sets modified14=1 and deep-assigns +C into +4 only. It does not invoke slot0 or alter current44,preview48,tail4C or FontManager.",
    "Save A53C20/vslot35 is void ret0. It skips when modified14=0 and clears that flag before the store. Its SEH catch consumes failure. Neither normal return nor dirty0 proves persistence; final export acceptance remains necessary.",
    "Save writes current44,preview48,language ID vector28,definitions34,text map4,tail4C to MCGSLINGUIST. No current-language/preview setter is called by this candidate."
  ]
